{"chunk_id": "bdeab7643a7e", "text": "After celestial nymphs fail to disturb the ascetic three\u2011headed son of Twashtri, Indra decides to eliminate the potential threat. He strikes the ascetic with his thunderbolt and, still fearful of the corpse\u2019s lingering power, orders a carpenter to sever the heads. From the three mouths burst different birds, symbolizing the being\u2019s varied practices. Twashtri, enraged at the unjust killing of his innocent son, creates the mighty demon Vritra to destroy Indra. Vritra nearly defeats the gods, even swallowing Indra, until the gods seek Vishnu\u2019s aid. Through diplomacy and deception, Indra exploits a loophole in Vritra\u2019s protective boon and kills him with sea\u2011foam infused with Vishnu\u2019s power. Yet victory brings no peace: Indra is overwhelmed by guilt and the sin of Brahmanicide, hides himself, and the cosmos falls into disorder without a king of the gods.\nIndra kills the three\u2011headed ascetic, provoking Twashtri to create Vritra; after struggle and deception aided by Vishnu, Indra slays Vritra but is overwhelmed by guilt.\nThemes: divine conflict, deception and loopholes, cosmic justice and guilt, creation of Vritra, divine intervention", "vector": [0.0025738689582794905, -0.003888725070282817, -0.006630124058574438, 0.017775094136595726, 0.007662379182875156, 0.04001765325665474, -0.03024338185787201, -0.016123486682772636, 0.004572382662445307, -0.01643485575914383, 0.008738631382584572, 0.013984518125653267, 0.005195119883865118, -0.006278141867369413, 0.0011253273114562035, 0.019859911873936653, 0.03527943417429924, -0.02122722566127777, 0.03641660511493683, -0.010674533434212208, -0.007804525550454855, 0.01740957424044609, -0.011243119835853577, 0.017924010753631592, -0.019467316567897797, -0.009483208879828453, 0.007378085982054472, -0.018885191529989243, 0.004748373758047819, -0.010992670431733131, 0.010857293382287025, -0.008264809846878052, 0.005794166587293148, -0.00387180270627141, -0